body:
Found while implementing objectstack#9326 (objectstack PR #9425), which fixes the producer half of this in `@objectstack/rest`. Filed separately because the fix lands here, in `objectui`.

## The measurement

`packages/app-shell/src/views/metadata-admin/ResourceEditPage.tsx` — the References tab loader (around line 793; **locate it by text, not by line number**):

```ts
setRefsLoading(true);
try {
  const r = await client.references(type, name);
  setRefs(r);
} catch (err) {
  setRefs([]);
  console.error('references() failed', err);
} finally {
  setRefsLoading(false);
}
```

`setRefs([])` is the same state a **successful** call returning zero references produces. And `ReferencesPanel` renders that state as, verbatim from `metadata-admin/i18n.ts`:

```
'engine.edit.refsEmptyDesc': 'Nothing in the metadata graph points at this item. Safe to delete.'
```

So **any** failure — the server refused, the network dropped, the session expired, the response was unparseable — is shown to the operator as an affirmative, measured statement that nothing depends on this item, and that deleting it is safe. The only trace is a `console.error` nobody is looking at. The user is typically on this panel *because* they are about to delete something.

`MetadataClient.references()` (`packages/data-objectstack/src/metadata-client.ts`) does its half correctly: it returns `[]` only for a `404`, and throws `parseError(res)` for every other non-ok status. The information reaches this component intact and is discarded here.

## Why now

`@objectstack/rest` used to answer `200 {references: []}` when the resolved protocol had no `findReferencesToMeta` method — a capability gap rendered as "nothing depends on this item". objectstack#9326 / PR #9425 changes that branch to refuse:

```
501  { error: { code: 'NOT_IMPLEMENTED', message: '...' } }
```

That makes the **wire** honest. It does not by itself remove the user-visible harm, because this `catch` turns the truthful `501` straight back into "Safe to delete." The producer fix is necessary and not sufficient; this is the other half.

**Not blocked by it, though.** The `catch` swallows failures today, for every cause listed above, and can be fixed independently of what the server sends.

## What would close it

An error state distinct from the empty state. Note that the current shape has no room for one: `ReferencesPanel` reads `refs == null` as *still loading* —

```ts
if (loading || refs == null) return <spinner/>;
if (refs.length === 0) return <Empty>…Safe to delete…</Empty>;
```

— so simply *not* setting `refs` on failure leaves a permanent spinner, and `setRefs([])` is the lie. A third state is needed (an `error` field, or a discriminated union for the panel's data), plus copy for it. Suggested shape, not asserted: the panel says the check could not be completed and offers a retry, and deliberately says nothing about whether deletion is safe — the honest answer when the question was not answered.

⚠️ Worth checking while in there whether the same `catch → empty` pattern appears on the sibling tabs this page loads (history, audit, diagnostics). A zero there needs its own control query before it is reported as a zero.

## Related

objectstack#9326 / objectstack PR #9425 (the producer half — the REST route now refuses instead of answering empty) · objectstack#9426 (the same producer-side defect class on the audit route) · ADR-0110 D3, "a miss and a fault are different facts"

## Dedup

Searched open issues here for the references panel, the "Safe to delete" empty state, and `ResourceEditPage` error handling; nothing covering this. Control query on the same repo (`metadata admin resource edit page`) returned three real, related cards (#4308, #4518, #4132, all closed), so the zero above is a measurement rather than a broken search. No duplicate.
